# NEXUS §126 — ASK THE RINGS: the WP5 lockstep link

Prediction SHA-256: `b706f2ac615ca016ad985c7e513cc73d2e20139d1583d47ddeaed8db13ea8c8e`

## Question
§121 left nine balanced lanes OPEN because the reader-ring and field-ring periods share a factor. This run does not revisit §124. It reconstructs the two actual CRT parent rings and their phase-compatible joint orbit.

## Result
Exact reconstruction passes: 10/10 invariants.
Eligible partial lanes: 804; balanced: 75; independent: 692; independent balanced: 66; lockstep of all kinds: 112; balanced lockstep: 9.
The paired orbit has period `lcm(h1,h2)`, and reachable phase addresses satisfy `i ≡ j (mod gcd(h1,h2))`. Thus the joint orbit is a phase-constrained subset of the Cartesian product when the periods share a factor.
All nine balanced lockstep cases have joint lean exactly zero and exactly reproduce their original rational-ring `mu - 1/2`: 9/9.
Among the nine, Cartesian-product lean differs from the joint route in 5/9 cases. The joint phase is therefore needed for those cases; the marginal rings alone do not specify the realized pairing.

